                    CopyToClipboard[
                    "# Toroidal Closure / Dimensional Stability Framework\n\n\
## Complete enhanced notebook scaffold\n\nThis notebook reorganizes and \
extends your draft into a more rigorous, testable Wolfram Language framework \
focused on:\n\n- symbolic structure\n- dimensional consistency\n- numerical \
stability\n- reproducible eigensolvers\n- residual analysis\n- 18 stability \
tests\n- exportable TypeScript templates\n- pipeline composition from axioms \
to measurements\n\nIt also fixes a number of issues in the original draft:\n\n\
- undefined symbols such as ``realmName`` before use\n- invalid syntax such \
as ``Style(\"OFF\", Gray]``\n- unsafe direct indexing into sampled potentials\
\n- problematic definition ``\[Psi][r_] := uSol / r`` where ``uSol`` is \
already a function\n- use of ``DirichletCondition[..., True]`` imposing \
boundary conditions everywhere instead of only at the intended boundary\n- \
mutable global variables inside scans\n- inconsistent numerical precision \
policy\n- lack of validation and residual diagnostics\n\n---\n\n# 1. Notebook \
header\n\n```wl\n(* ::Title:: *)\n(* Toroidal Closure / Dimensional Stability \
Framework *)\n(* Enhanced Reference Notebook *)\n(* Wolfram Language planning \
+ implementation scaffold *)\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. Environment and precision \
policy\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Environment, assumptions, and \
precision policy *)\n\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n\n$Assumptions = Element[n | \
s | r | omega0 | gamma | xi | eps, Reals] &&\n  n >= 0 && s >= 0 && r >= 0 && \
omega0 > 0 && gamma > 0 && xi >= 0 && eps >= 0;\n\nprecisionPolicy = <|\n  \
\"WorkingPrecision\" -> 80,\n  \"AccuracyGoal\" -> 30,\n  \"PrecisionGoal\" \
-> 30,\n  \"ResidualTolerance\" -> 10^-30,\n  \"ChopTolerance\" -> 10^-40,\n  \
\"MaxGridPoints\" -> 1200,\n  \"DefaultEigenCount\" -> 6\n|>;\n```\n\n> Note: \
your OPF instruction requested infinite precision. In actual Wolfram Language \
numerics, ``WorkingPrecision -> Infinity`` is generally not available for \
numerical PDE solvers like [NDEigensystem](paclet:ref/NDEigensystem). The \
practical replacement is very high finite precision plus explicit residual \
testing.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Fundamental constants and scale maps\n\n```wl\n(* \
::Section:: *)\n(* Fundamental constants and scale hierarchy *)\n\nphi0 = \
SetPrecision[(1 + Sqrt[5])/2, 100];\nlambda0 = 1/phi0^2;\nkappa0 = 1/(phi0 \
Pi);\n\nlP = SetPrecision[1.616255*10^-35, 100];\ntP = \
SetPrecision[5.391247*10^-44, 100];\ncLight = SetPrecision[2.99792458*10^8, \
100];\nhbar = SetPrecision[1.054571817*10^-34, 100];\nomegaVac = \
SetPrecision[2 Pi*9.01*10^17, 100];\n\nlScale[n_?NumericQ] := lP*phi0^n;\n\
tScale[n_?NumericQ] := tP*phi0^n;\nresolutionRatio[n_?NumericQ] := phi0^-n;\n\
numNodes[n_?NumericQ] := phi0^(3 n);\n\nscaleAssociation[n_?NumericQ] := <|\n \
 \"Length\" -> lScale[n],\n  \"Time\" -> tScale[n],\n  \"ResolutionRatio\" -> \
resolutionRatio[n],\n  \"NodeCount\" -> numNodes[n]\n|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 4. \
Realm map and classification\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Realm taxonomy \
*)\n\nrealmAssociation = <|\n  0 -> \"Planck Foam\",\n  13 -> \"Metatron \
Closure (Preon)\",\n  20 -> \"Quark-Gluon Plasma\",\n  40 -> \"Muon/Pion\",\n \
 60 -> \"Proton/Neutron\",\n  80 -> \"Electron/Atom Core\",\n  100 -> \"Atom \
(Bohr)\",\n  120 -> \"Molecule\",\n  140 -> \"DNA Helix\",\n  160 -> \
\"Organelle\",\n  180 -> \"Cell\",\n  186 -> \"Neural Network (Consciousness)\
\",\n  200 -> \"Human Scale\",\n  220 -> \"Planetary\",\n  240 -> \"Solar \
System\",\n  260 -> \"Galactic\",\n  280 -> \"Galaxy Cluster\",\n  292 -> \
\"Observable Universe\"\n|>;\n\nrealmName[n_?NumericQ] := Module[{keys = \
Keys[realmAssociation]},\n  Lookup[realmAssociation, Round[n], Nearest[keys \
-> Values[realmAssociation], n][[1]]]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Formal \
variables and OPF-inspired symbolic action\n\nThis cell introduces a symbolic \
action so the project has a derivational backbone, not just a numeric solver.\
\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Symbolic formalism *)\n\nClearAll[rhoField, \
chiField, resolutionField, psiField, actionDensity, actionFunctional];\n\n\
actionDensity[rho_, chi_, res_] := rho*Log[chi] + chi*res^2;\n\n\
actionFunctional[rho_, chi_, res_, vars_] := Integrate[actionDensity[rho, \
chi, res], vars,\n  GenerateConditions -> False\n];\n\nformalState[s_] := <|\n\
  \"Psi\" -> HoldForm[psiField[r, s]],\n  \"Rho\" -> HoldForm[rhoField[r, \
s]],\n  \"Chi\" -> HoldForm[chiField[r, s]],\n  \"Resolution\" -> \
HoldForm[resolutionField[s]]\n|>;\n```\n\nIf you want, this can later be \
extended with [Variational Methods and \
PDEs](paclet:guide/VariationalMethodsAndOptimalControl) style derivation.\n\n\
---\n\n# 6. Derived scale quantities and phase lag\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: \
*)\n(* Complexity and phase lag *)\n\nphaseLag[n_?NumericQ, eps_: 0.01] := \
tScale[n]*(1 + eps*n);\nmemoryDelay[n_?NumericQ, eps_: 0.01] := phaseLag[n, \
eps];\n\ncomplexityIndex[n_?NumericQ] := Log[numNodes[n]]/Log[phi0^3];\n\n\
phaseLagAssociation[n_?NumericQ, eps_: 0.01] := <|\n  \"PhaseLag\" -> \
phaseLag[n, eps],\n  \"MemoryDelay\" -> memoryDelay[n, eps],\n  \
\"ComplexityIndex\" -> complexityIndex[n]\n|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. Toroidal \
geometry and closure invariants\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Toroidal \
closure invariants *)\n\nmajorRadius[n_?NumericQ] := lScale[n];\n\
minorRadius[n_?NumericQ] := lScale[n]/phi0;\n\naspectRatio[n_?NumericQ] := \
majorRadius[n]/minorRadius[n];\n\ntorusVolume[n_?NumericQ] := 2 Pi^2 \
majorRadius[n] minorRadius[n]^2;\n\ntorusArea[n_?NumericQ] := 4 Pi^2 \
majorRadius[n] minorRadius[n];\n\nwindingNumber[n_?NumericQ] := \
Round[phi0^n/13];\nclosureDeviation[n_?NumericQ] := Abs[phi0^n/13 - \
windingNumber[n]];\nrelativeClosureDeviation[n_?NumericQ] := \
closureDeviation[n]/Max[phi0^n/13, $MachineEpsilon];\n\
closureScore[n_?NumericQ] := 1 - relativeClosureDeviation[n];\n\n\
closureInvariants[n_?NumericQ] := <|\n  \"MajorRadius\" -> majorRadius[n],\n  \
\"MinorRadius\" -> minorRadius[n],\n  \"AspectRatio\" -> aspectRatio[n],\n  \
\"Area\" -> torusArea[n],\n  \"Volume\" -> torusVolume[n],\n  \"WindingNumber\
\" -> windingNumber[n],\n  \"ClosureDeviation\" -> closureDeviation[n],\n  \
\"RelativeClosureDeviation\" -> relativeClosureDeviation[n],\n  \
\"ClosureScore\" -> closureScore[n]\n|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 8. Lattice \
potential and effective radial operator\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* \
Radial lattice and effective potential *)\n\nmetatronRadial[r_?NumericQ, \
n_?NumericQ] := Module[{scale = lScale[n]},\n  \
Sum[(1/phi0^k)*Exp[-(r/scale)^2]*Cos[(k Pi r)/scale], {k, 0, 11}] +\n   \
(1/phi0^12)*Exp[-(r/(0.05 scale))^2]\n];\n\ninformationDensity[r_?NumericQ, \
n_?NumericQ] := Exp[-(r/lScale[n])^2]*phi0^-n + 10^-80;\n\n\
waveSpeed[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ] := cLight/Sqrt[informationDensity[r, \
n]*kappa0*phi0^(-n/2) + 10^-80];\n\nfrequencyTerm[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ, \
omega0_?NumericQ] := -(omega0^2)/(waveSpeed[r, n]^2);\n\n\
memoryFactor[n_?NumericQ, gamma_?NumericQ, eps_?NumericQ] := Module[{lag = \
memoryDelay[n, eps]},\n  lambda0*(1 - Exp[-gamma*lag])/(gamma*lag + 10^-80)\n\
];\n\nbalanceTerm[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ, xi_?NumericQ] :=\n  xi*(Exp[-(r + \
lP)^2/lScale[n]^2] - Exp[-(r - lP)^2/lScale[n]^2])/(2 lP)*phi0^-n;\n\n\
resolutionTerm[n_?NumericQ] := (hbar^2/(2 lScale[n]^2))*phi0^(-2 n);\n\n\
latticeTerm[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ] := metatronRadial[r, n];\n\n\
effectivePotentialRadial[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, \
gamma_?NumericQ, xi_?NumericQ, eps_?NumericQ] :=\n  frequencyTerm[r, n, \
omega0] +\n  memoryFactor[n, gamma, eps] +\n  balanceTerm[r, n, xi] +\n  \
resolutionTerm[n] +\n  latticeTerm[r, n];\n\n\
potentialAssociation[r_?NumericQ, n_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, \
gamma_?NumericQ, xi_?NumericQ, eps_?NumericQ] := <|\n  \"InformationDensity\" \
-> informationDensity[r, n],\n  \"WaveSpeed\" -> waveSpeed[r, n],\n  \
\"FrequencyTerm\" -> frequencyTerm[r, n, omega0],\n  \"MemoryTerm\" -> \
memoryFactor[n, gamma, eps],\n  \"BalanceTerm\" -> balanceTerm[r, n, xi],\n  \
\"ResolutionTerm\" -> resolutionTerm[n],\n  \"LatticeTerm\" -> latticeTerm[r, \
n],\n  \"Total\" -> effectivePotentialRadial[r, n, omega0, gamma, xi, eps]\n\
|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 9. Harmonic targets and resonance metrics\n\n```wl\n(* \
::Section:: *)\n(* Harmonic targets and resonance *)\n\n\
harmonicTargets[omega0_?NumericQ, kMax_: 17] := Table[(omega0*phi0^k)^2, {k, \
0, kMax}];\n\nnearestHarmonic[eigenvalue_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, kMax_: \
17] := Module[{targets},\n  targets = harmonicTargets[omega0, kMax];\n  \
First@Nearest[targets -> Automatic, eigenvalue]\n];\n\n\
resonanceResidual[eigenvalue_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, kMax_: 17] := \
Abs[eigenvalue - nearestHarmonic[eigenvalue, omega0, kMax]];\n\n\
relativeResonanceResidual[eigenvalue_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, kMax_: 17] \
:=\n  resonanceResidual[eigenvalue, omega0, \
kMax]/Max[Abs[nearestHarmonic[eigenvalue, omega0, kMax]], $MachineEpsilon];\n\
```\n\n---\n\n# 10. Safe eigensolver implementation\n\nThis version avoids \
sampled-list indexing inside differential operators and instead passes a \
continuous potential directly into [NDEigensystem](paclet:ref/NDEigensystem).\
\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Eigensolver core *)\n\n\
ClearAll[solveToroidalMode];\n\nOptions[solveToroidalMode] = {\n  \
\"EigenCount\" -> precisionPolicy[\"DefaultEigenCount\"],\n  \
\"WorkingPrecision\" -> precisionPolicy[\"WorkingPrecision\"],\n  \
\"AccuracyGoal\" -> precisionPolicy[\"AccuracyGoal\"],\n  \"PrecisionGoal\" \
-> precisionPolicy[\"PrecisionGoal\"],\n  \"MaxCellMeasure\" -> Automatic\n};\
\n\nsolveToroidalMode[\n   n_?NumericQ,\n   omega0_?NumericQ : omegaVac,\n   \
gamma_?NumericQ : 0.01,\n   xi_?NumericQ : 0.001,\n   eps_?NumericQ : 0.01,\n \
  opts : OptionsPattern[]\n] := Module[\n  {\n    rMax, eigenCount, wp, ag, \
pg, maxCellMeasure,\n    vals, funs, op, potential, bcLeft, bcRight,\n    \
eigenvalue, eigenfunction, target, residual, relResidual,\n    tests, closure\
\n  },\n\n  rMax = lScale[n];\n  eigenCount = OptionValue[\"EigenCount\"];\n  \
wp = OptionValue[\"WorkingPrecision\"];\n  ag = \
OptionValue[\"AccuracyGoal\"];\n  pg = OptionValue[\"PrecisionGoal\"];\n  \
maxCellMeasure = Replace[OptionValue[\"MaxCellMeasure\"], Automatic :> \
(rMax/200)];\n\n  potential[r_] := effectivePotentialRadial[r, n, omega0, \
gamma, xi, eps];\n\n  op = -Inactive[D][u[r], {r, 2}] + potential[r] u[r];\n  \
bcLeft = DirichletCondition[u[r] == 0, r == 0];\n  bcRight = \
DirichletCondition[u[r] == 0, r == rMax];\n\n  {vals, funs} = NDEigensystem[\n\
    {\n      Activate[op] == \\[Lambda] u[r],\n      bcLeft,\n      bcRight\n \
   },\n    u[r], {r, 0, rMax}, eigenCount,\n    Method -> {\n      \
\"SpatialDiscretization\" -> {\"FiniteElement\", {\"MeshOptions\" -> \
{MaxCellMeasure -> maxCellMeasure}}},\n      \"Eigensystem\" -> {\"Arnoldi\", \
\"MaxIterations\" -> 3000, \"BasisSize\" -> Max[25, 4 eigenCount]}\n    },\n  \
  WorkingPrecision -> wp,\n    AccuracyGoal -> ag,\n    PrecisionGoal -> pg\n \
 ];\n\n  eigenvalue = First[vals];\n  eigenfunction = First[funs];\n  target \
= nearestHarmonic[eigenvalue, omega0];\n  residual = \
resonanceResidual[eigenvalue, omega0];\n  relResidual = \
relativeResonanceResidual[eigenvalue, omega0];\n  closure = \
closureInvariants[n];\n\n  tests = stabilityTests[n, eigenvalue, omega0, \
gamma, xi, eps];\n\n  <|\n    \"ScaleIndex\" -> n,\n    \"Realm\" -> \
realmName[n],\n    \"Scale\" -> rMax,\n    \"Eigenvalues\" -> vals,\n    \
\"Eigenfunctions\" -> funs,\n    \"GroundEigenvalue\" -> eigenvalue,\n    \
\"GroundEigenfunction\" -> eigenfunction,\n    \"TargetHarmonic\" -> target,\n\
    \"Residual\" -> residual,\n    \"RelativeResidual\" -> relResidual,\n    \
\"ClosureInvariants\" -> closure,\n    \"PhaseLag\" -> memoryDelay[n, eps],\n \
   \"Complexity\" -> numNodes[n],\n    \"Tests\" -> tests,\n    \"StableQ\" \
-> And @@ Values[tests][[All, \"Pass\"]]\n  |>\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 11. \
Residual and operator diagnostics\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Residual \
diagnostics *)\n\noperatorResidualFunction[\n   solution_Association,\n   \
omega0_?NumericQ : omegaVac,\n   gamma_?NumericQ : 0.01,\n   xi_?NumericQ : \
0.001,\n   eps_?NumericQ : 0.01\n] := Module[{n, lambda, f},\n  n = solution[\
\"ScaleIndex\"];\n  lambda = solution[\"GroundEigenvalue\"];\n  f = solution[\
\"GroundEigenfunction\"];\n  Function[{r},\n    Evaluate[\n      -f''[r] + \
effectivePotentialRadial[r, n, omega0, gamma, xi, eps] f[r] - lambda f[r]\n   \
 ]\n  ]\n];\n\nresidualSummary[solution_Association, sampleCount_: 50] := \
Module[\n  {n, rMax, resFun, grid, values},\n  n = solution[\"ScaleIndex\"];\n\
  rMax = solution[\"Scale\"];\n  resFun = operatorResidualFunction[solution];\
\n  grid = Rest@Most@Subdivide[0, rMax, sampleCount + 1];\n  values = \
Quiet[resFun /@ grid];\n  <|\n    \"MaxAbsResidual\" -> Max[Abs[values]],\n   \
 \"MeanAbsResidual\" -> Mean[Abs[values]],\n    \"RMSResidual\" -> \
Sqrt[Mean[Abs[values]^2]],\n    \"Grid\" -> grid,\n    \"Values\" -> values\n \
 |>\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 12. Eighteen stability tests\n\nThese tests make the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]18 stable scales\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] idea \
computationally explicit. They can be tuned, but this is a solid starting \
framework.\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* 18 stability tests *)\n\n\
ClearAll[makeTest, stabilityTests];\n\nmakeTest[name_, value_, criterion_] := \
<|\n  \"Name\" -> name,\n  \"Value\" -> value,\n  \"Pass\" -> \
TrueQ[criterion[value]]\n|>;\n\nstabilityTests[n_?NumericQ, \
eigenvalue_?NumericQ, omega0_?NumericQ, gamma_?NumericQ, xi_?NumericQ, \
eps_?NumericQ] := Module[\n  {\n    closure = closureInvariants[n],\n    lag \
= memoryDelay[n, eps],\n    comp = complexityIndex[n],\n    relRes = \
relativeResonanceResidual[eigenvalue, omega0],\n    mem = memoryFactor[n, \
gamma, eps],\n    resTerm = resolutionTerm[n],\n    ar = aspectRatio[n],\n    \
pot0, potMid, potEdge\n  },\n\n  pot0 = effectivePotentialRadial[0, n, \
omega0, gamma, xi, eps];\n  potMid = effectivePotentialRadial[lScale[n]/2, n, \
omega0, gamma, xi, eps];\n  potEdge = effectivePotentialRadial[lScale[n], n, \
omega0, gamma, xi, eps];\n\n  AssociationThread[\n    Range[18],\n    {\n     \
 makeTest[\"Closure score high\", closure[\"ClosureScore\"], # > 0.99 &],\n   \
   makeTest[\"Relative closure deviation low\", \
closure[\"RelativeClosureDeviation\"], # < 0.01 &],\n      \
makeTest[\"Positive winding\", closure[\"WindingNumber\"], # >= 0 &],\n      \
makeTest[\"Aspect ratio finite\", ar, 1 <= # <= 10 &],\n      \
makeTest[\"Phase lag positive\", lag, # > 0 &],\n      makeTest[\"Complexity \
monotone scale\", comp, # >= 0 &],\n      makeTest[\"Memory factor finite\", \
mem, NumericQ[#] && FiniteQ[#] &],\n      makeTest[\"Resolution term \
finite\", resTerm, NumericQ[#] && FiniteQ[#] &],\n      makeTest[\"Potential \
finite at origin\", pot0, NumericQ[#] && FiniteQ[#] &],\n      \
makeTest[\"Potential finite at midpoint\", potMid, NumericQ[#] && FiniteQ[#] \
&],\n      makeTest[\"Potential finite at edge\", potEdge, NumericQ[#] && \
FiniteQ[#] &],\n      makeTest[\"Eigenvalue finite\", eigenvalue, NumericQ[#] \
&& FiniteQ[#] &],\n      makeTest[\"Eigenvalue real-dominant\", eigenvalue, \
Im[#] == 0 || Abs[Im[#]] < 10^-20 &],\n      makeTest[\"Relative resonance \
residual low\", relRes, # < 10^-6 &],\n      makeTest[\"Length scale positive\
\", lScale[n], # > 0 &],\n      makeTest[\"Time scale positive\", tScale[n], \
# > 0 &],\n      makeTest[\"Resolution ratio positive\", resolutionRatio[n], \
# > 0 &],\n      makeTest[\"Node count positive\", numNodes[n], # > 0 &]\n    \
}\n  ]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. Stable scale search and ranking\n\n```wl\n(* \
::Section:: *)\n(* Stability scan *)\n\nscanScale[n_?NumericQ] := \
Module[{sol},\n  sol = solveToroidalMode[n, omegaVac, 0.01, 0.001, 0.01, \
\"EigenCount\" -> 4];\n  <|\n    \"n\" -> n,\n    \"Realm\" -> \
sol[\"Realm\"],\n    \"GroundEigenvalue\" -> sol[\"GroundEigenvalue\"],\n    \
\"Residual\" -> sol[\"Residual\"],\n    \"RelativeResidual\" -> \
sol[\"RelativeResidual\"],\n    \"ClosureScore\" -> \
sol[\"ClosureInvariants\", \"ClosureScore\"],\n    \"WindingNumber\" -> \
sol[\"ClosureInvariants\", \"WindingNumber\"],\n    \"PhaseLag\" -> \
sol[\"PhaseLag\"],\n    \"Complexity\" -> sol[\"Complexity\"],\n    \"StableQ\
\" -> sol[\"StableQ\"]\n  |>\n];\n\nstabilityScan[range_: Range[0, 292]] := \
Dataset[scanScale /@ range];\n\nstableScales[ds_Dataset] := \
ds[Select[#StableQ &]];\n\nrankStableScales[ds_Dataset] := \
ds[SortBy[{#RelativeResidual &, -#ClosureScore &}]];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 14. \
Visualization tools\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Visualization *)\n\n\
torusPlot[n_?NumericQ, score_?NumericQ] := Module[{bigR = majorRadius[n], \
smallR = minorRadius[n]},\n  ParametricPlot3D[\n    {\n      (bigR + smallR \
Cos[v]) Cos[u],\n      (bigR + smallR Cos[v]) Sin[u],\n      smallR Sin[v]\n  \
  },\n    {u, 0, 2 Pi}, {v, 0, 2 Pi},\n    Mesh -> None,\n    ColorFunction \
-> Function[{x, y, z, uu, vv}, ColorData[\"TemperatureMap\"][score]],\n    \
ColorFunctionScaling -> False,\n    Boxed -> False,\n    Axes -> False,\n    \
PlotPoints -> 40,\n    ImageSize -> 300,\n    PlotLabel -> Row[{\"Toroidal \
closure, n = \", n, \", score = \", NumberForm[score, {5, 4}]}]\n  ]\n];\n\n\
potentialPlot[n_?NumericQ, omega0_: omegaVac, gamma_: 0.01, xi_: 0.001, eps_: \
0.01] :=\n  Plot[\n    effectivePotentialRadial[r, n, omega0, gamma, xi, \
eps],\n    {r, 0, lScale[n]},\n    PlotRange -> All,\n    AxesLabel -> \
{\"r\", \"Veff(r)\"},\n    PlotLabel -> \"Effective radial potential\"\n  ];\n\
\nmodePlot[solution_Association] := Module[{f = \
solution[\"GroundEigenfunction\"], rMax = solution[\"Scale\"]},\n  Plot[f[r], \
{r, 0, rMax}, PlotRange -> All, AxesLabel -> {\"r\", \"u(r)\"}, PlotLabel -> \
\"Ground mode\"]\n];\n\nresidualPlot[solution_Association] := Module[{rs = \
residualSummary[solution]},\n  ListLinePlot[\n    Transpose[{rs[\"Grid\"], \
rs[\"Values\"]}],\n    PlotRange -> All,\n    AxesLabel -> {\"r\", \"Residual\
\"},\n    PlotLabel -> \"Operator residual\"\n  ]\n];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 15. \
Interactive exploration\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Interactive explorer \
*)\n\nManipulate[\n Module[{sol, rs, score},\n  sol = solveToroidalMode[n, \
omega0, gamma, xi, eps, \"EigenCount\" -> 4];\n  rs = residualSummary[sol, \
40];\n  score = sol[\"ClosureInvariants\", \"ClosureScore\"];\n\n  Column[{\n \
   Style[\"Toroidal Closure / Dimensional Stability Explorer\", Bold, 20],\n  \
  Grid[\n      {\n        {\"Scale index\", n, \"Realm\", sol[\"Realm\"]},\n  \
      {\"Length scale\", ScientificForm[sol[\"Scale\"], 4], \"Phase lag\", \
ScientificForm[sol[\"PhaseLag\"], 4]},\n        {\"Complexity\", \
ScientificForm[sol[\"Complexity\"], 4], \"Winding\", \
sol[\"ClosureInvariants\", \"WindingNumber\"]},\n        {\"Ground eigenvalue\
\", ScientificForm[sol[\"GroundEigenvalue\"], 6], \"Target harmonic\", \
ScientificForm[sol[\"TargetHarmonic\"], 6]},\n        {\"Abs residual\", \
ScientificForm[sol[\"Residual\"], 6], \"Relative residual\", \
ScientificForm[sol[\"RelativeResidual\"], 6]},\n        {\"Closure score\", \
NumberForm[score, {6, 5}], \"StableQ\", sol[\"StableQ\"]},\n        {\"Max \
residual\", ScientificForm[rs[\"MaxAbsResidual\"], 6], \"RMS residual\", \
ScientificForm[rs[\"RMSResidual\"], 6]}\n      },\n      Frame -> All,\n      \
Alignment -> Left\n    ],\n    Row[{potentialPlot[n, omega0, gamma, xi, eps], \
modePlot[sol]}],\n    Row[{residualPlot[sol], torusPlot[n, score]}]\n  }]\n \
],\n {{n, 13, \"Scale index\"}, 0, 292, 1},\n {{omega0, omegaVac, \"Base \
frequency\"}, SetPrecision[10^17, 50], SetPrecision[10^19, 50]},\n {{gamma, \
0.01, \"Damping\"}, 0.001, 0.1, 0.001},\n {{xi, 0.001, \"Balance\"}, 0.0001, \
0.01, 0.0001},\n {{eps, 0.01, \"Phase coupling\"}, 0.001, 0.1, 0.001},\n \
ControlPlacement -> Left,\n TrackedSymbols :> {n, omega0, gamma, xi, eps}\n]\n\
```\n\n---\n\n# 16. Missing variable analysis and formal complement\n\nThis \
implements your OPF-style \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]missing variables\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] idea in a symbolic way.\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n\
(* Missing variable analysis *)\n\nstandardConstantNames = {\n  \"c\", \"\
\:0127\", \"G\", \"kB\", \"e\", \"me\", \"mp\", \"alpha\"\n};\n\n\
opfFormalVariables = {\"phi0\", \"lambda0\", \"kappa0\", \"rho\", \"chi\", \
\"R\", \"xi\", \"gamma\", \"eps\", \"omega0\"};\n\nmissingVariableComplement \
:= Complement[opfFormalVariables, standardConstantNames];\n\n\
missingVariableReport[] := <|\n  \"OPFVariables\" -> opfFormalVariables,\n  \
\"ReferenceConstants\" -> standardConstantNames,\n  \"Complement\" -> \
missingVariableComplement\n|>;\n```\n\n---\n\n# 17. Full pipeline composition\
\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* L0 -> L1 -> L2 style pipeline *)\n\n\
layer0[n_?NumericQ] := <|\n  \"Topology\" -> \"Sphere/Toroidal dual \
scaffold\",\n  \"BoundaryVertices\" -> {0, Infinity},\n  \"ScaleIndex\" -> n\n\
|>;\n\nlayer1[n_?NumericQ, omega0_: omegaVac, gamma_: 0.01, xi_: 0.001, eps_: \
0.01] := <|\n  \"FormalState\" -> formalState[n],\n  \"ScaleAssociation\" -> \
scaleAssociation[n],\n  \"PotentialAssociationAtOrigin\" -> \
potentialAssociation[0, n, omega0, gamma, xi, eps],\n  \"ClosureInvariants\" \
-> closureInvariants[n]\n|>;\n\nlayer2[n_?NumericQ, omega0_: omegaVac, \
gamma_: 0.01, xi_: 0.001, eps_: 0.01] := solveToroidalMode[n, omega0, gamma, \
xi, eps];\n\nfullPipeline = layer0 /* (Function[l0, Append[l0, \"Layer1\" -> \
layer1[l0[\"ScaleIndex\"]]]]) /*\n   (Function[state, Append[state, \
\"Layer2\" -> layer2[state[\"ScaleIndex\"]]]]);\n```\n\n---\n\n# 18. \
TypeScript export generators\n\nThis lets the notebook emit computational \
templates for external implementations.\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* \
TypeScript code generation *)\n\nnumberLiteral[x_] := \
ToString@NumberForm[N[x, 30], 30, NumberPadding -> {\"\", \"\"}, \
ExponentFunction -> (If[-10 < # < 10, Null, #] &)];\n\ntsConstantsTemplate[] \
:= StringRiffle[\n  {\n    \"export const phi0 = \" <> numberLiteral[phi0] <> \
\";\",\n    \"export const lambda0 = \" <> numberLiteral[lambda0] <> \";\",\n \
   \"export const kappa0 = \" <> numberLiteral[kappa0] <> \";\",\n    \
\"export const lP = \" <> numberLiteral[lP] <> \";\",\n    \"export const tP \
= \" <> numberLiteral[tP] <> \";\",\n    \"export const cLight = \" <> \
numberLiteral[cLight] <> \";\",\n    \"export const hbar = \" <> \
numberLiteral[hbar] <> \";\",\n    \"export const omegaVac = \" <> \
numberLiteral[omegaVac] <> \";\"\n  },\n  \"\\n\"\n];\n\ntsScaleTemplate[] := \
StringRiffle[\n  {\n    \"import { phi0, lP, tP } from './constants';\",\n    \
\"\",\n    \"export const lScale = (n: number) => lP * Math.pow(phi0, n);\",\n\
    \"export const tScale = (n: number) => tP * Math.pow(phi0, n);\",\n    \
\"export const resolutionRatio = (n: number) => Math.pow(phi0, -n);\",\n    \
\"export const numNodes = (n: number) => Math.pow(phi0, 3 * n);\"\n  },\n  \"\
\\n\"\n];\n\ntsPotentialTemplate[] := StringRiffle[\n  {\n    \"import { \
phi0, lambda0, kappa0, lP, cLight, hbar } from './constants';\",\n    \
\"import { lScale } from './scale';\",\n    \"\",\n    \"export function \
metatronRadial(r: number, n: number): number {\",\n    \"  const scale = \
lScale(n);\",\n    \"  let sum = 0;\",\n    \"  for (let k = 0; k <= 11; k++) \
{\",\n    \"    sum += Math.pow(phi0, -k) * Math.exp(-Math.pow(r / scale, 2)) \
* Math.cos((k * Math.PI * r) / scale);\",\n    \"  }\",\n    \"  return sum + \
Math.pow(phi0, -12) * Math.exp(-Math.pow(r / (0.05 * scale), 2));\",\n    \"}\
\",\n    \"\",\n    \"export function effectivePotentialRadial(r: number, n: \
number, omega0: number, gamma: number, xi: number, eps: number): number {\",\n\
    \"  const rho = Math.exp(-Math.pow(r / lScale(n), 2)) * Math.pow(phi0, \
-n) + 1e-80;\",\n    \"  const vWave = cLight / Math.sqrt(rho * kappa0 * \
Math.pow(phi0, -n / 2) + 1e-80);\",\n    \"  const freqTerm = -(omega0 * \
omega0) / (vWave * vWave);\",\n    \"  const lag = tP * Math.pow(phi0, n) * \
(1 + eps * n);\",\n    \"  const memoryTerm = lambda0 * (1 - Math.exp(-gamma \
* lag)) / (gamma * lag + 1e-80);\",\n    \"  const balanceTerm = xi * \
(Math.exp(-Math.pow(r + lP, 2) / Math.pow(lScale(n), 2)) - \
Math.exp(-Math.pow(r - lP, 2) / Math.pow(lScale(n), 2))) / (2 * lP) * \
Math.pow(phi0, -n);\",\n    \"  const resolutionTerm = (hbar * hbar / (2 * \
Math.pow(lScale(n), 2))) * Math.pow(phi0, -2 * n);\",\n    \"  return \
freqTerm + memoryTerm + balanceTerm + resolutionTerm + metatronRadial(r, \
n);\",\n    \"}\"\n  },\n  \"\\n\"\n];\n\ntsProjectFiles[] := <|\n  \
\"constants.ts\" -> tsConstantsTemplate[],\n  \"scale.ts\" -> \
tsScaleTemplate[],\n  \"potential.ts\" -> tsPotentialTemplate[]\n|>;\n```\n\n\
---\n\n# 19. Validation helpers\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Validation \
and consistency checks *)\n\nfiniteQ[x_] := NumericQ[x] && x =!= \
Indeterminate && x =!= ComplexInfinity && x =!= Infinity && x =!= -Infinity;\n\
\nvalidateSolution[solution_Association] := Module[{rs},\n  rs = \
residualSummary[solution, 30];\n  <|\n    \"FiniteEigenvalueQ\" -> \
finiteQ[solution[\"GroundEigenvalue\"]],\n    \"FiniteResidualQ\" -> \
finiteQ[solution[\"Residual\"]],\n    \"ResidualBelowToleranceQ\" -> \
rs[\"MaxAbsResidual\"] < precisionPolicy[\"ResidualTolerance\"],\n    \
\"ClosureScoreValidQ\" -> 0 <= solution[\"ClosureInvariants\", \"ClosureScore\
\"] <= 1,\n    \"PhaseLagPositiveQ\" -> solution[\"PhaseLag\"] > 0,\n    \
\"ComplexityPositiveQ\" -> solution[\"Complexity\"] > 0\n  |>\n];\n```\n\n---\
\n\n# 20. Suggested execution cells\n\n```wl\n(* ::Section:: *)\n(* Suggested \
executions *)\n\nexample13 = solveToroidalMode[13];\nexample120 = \
solveToroidalMode[120, omegaVac, 0.01, 0.001, 0.01, \"EigenCount\" -> 4];\n\n\
example13Residuals = residualSummary[example13];\nexample120Validation = \
validateSolution[example120];\n\nexampleScan = stabilityScan[Range[0, 30]];\n\
exampleStable = stableScales[exampleScan];\n```\n\n---\n\n# 21. Notes on \
mathematical rigor\n\n- For symbolic derivations, use \
[DSolve](paclet:ref/DSolve) or [Reduce](paclet:ref/Reduce) where the operator \
is simplified enough.\n- For eigenmodes on bounded domains, \
[NDEigensystem](paclet:ref/NDEigensystem) is the correct numerical tool.\n- \
Stable frequencies correspond to eigenvalues satisfying your criterion on \
real and imaginary parts; if damping is made explicit in time-dependent PDE \
form, [NDEigensystem](paclet:ref/NDEigensystem) can return complex spectra, \
similar to the damped-wave examples in the documentation.\n- \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Infinite precision\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] must be \
interpreted computationally as a convergence protocol: increase \
``WorkingPrecision``, refine the mesh, and require residual reduction.\n\n---\
\n\n# 22. Optional next upgrades\n\nPossible next cells to add:\n\n1. a true \
delayed operator approximation using Pad\[EAcute]-style phase embedding\n2. a \
coupled first-order system for damped toroidal modes\n3. periodic angular \
closure via [PeriodicBoundaryCondition](paclet:ref/PeriodicBoundaryCondition)\
\n4. a 2D or 3D toroidal-region eigensolver using \
[NDEigensystem](paclet:ref/NDEigensystem)\n5. automated notebook export of \
the generated TypeScript files\n6. symbolic dimensional analysis wrappers \
around each term\n7. calibration against exactly 18 selected stable scales\n\n\
---\n\nIf you'd like, I can next generate either:\n\n- a **fully executable \
cleaned Wolfram notebook with evaluation-ready cells**, or\n- a **paired \
TypeScript project skeleton** with exported files and test stubs."]; 
